<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Alert triage economics</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #ffffff; --fg: #141617; --muted: #4a5154; --line: #d8dcde;
    --panel: #f5f6f7; --bad: #96201a; --ok: #17593a;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #121415; --fg: #e8eaeb; --muted: #9aa2a5; --line: #2a2e30;
      --panel: #1a1d1e; --bad: #ef6a5f; --ok: #4fb183;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg);
    font: 15px/1.55 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; }
  .wrap { max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 16px 64px; }
  h1 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 4px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h2 { font-size: 15px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    color: var(--muted); margin: 40px 0 12px; font-weight: 600; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 28px; font-size: 13px; }
  .headline { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 20px 22px;
    background: var(--panel); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .big { font-size: 42px; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1; color: var(--bad);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .big small { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 500; }
  .headline p { margin: 10px 0 0; max-width: 68ch; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; }
  .tile { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 14px; }
  .tile .n { font-size: 23px; font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .tile .l { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  figure { margin: 18px 0; }
  figure img { width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; }
  figcaption { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; margin-top: 8px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13.5px; }
  caption { text-align: left; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); padding-bottom: 10px; }
  th { text-align: left; font-size: 11.5px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 8px 10px 8px 0; font-weight: 600; }
  td { padding: 9px 10px 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  code { font: 12.5px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    background: var(--panel); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .v { font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; white-space: nowrap; }
  .v::before { margin-right: 6px; }
  .v-no { color: var(--bad); }
  .v-no::before { content: "x"; }
  .v-yes { color: var(--ok); }
  .v-yes::before { content: "ok"; font-size: 10px; }
  .v-unknown { color: var(--muted); }
  .v-unknown::before { content: "?"; }
  .ci { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .skip { position: absolute; left: -9999px; }
  .skip:focus { left: 8px; top: 8px; background: var(--bg); padding: 10px 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; z-index: 10; }
  footer { margin-top: 44px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#rules">Skip to the per rule table</a>
<div class="wrap">
  <h1>Alert triage economics</h1>
  <p class="sub">
    {{ "{:,}".format(stream.alerts) }} alerts, {{ "{:,}".format(stream.true_positives) }} true positives,
    one in {{ stream.one_in }}. {{ stream.rules_analysed }} rules analysed.
  </p>

  <div class="headline">
    <div class="big" role="img"
         aria-label="Removing half of every rule's volume costs {{ "%.1f"|format(stream.blanket_cut_cost['cut_50']) }} percent of true positives">
      {{ "%.1f"|format(stream.blanket_cut_cost['cut_50']) }}<small>%</small>
    </div>
    <p>
      of true positives are lost if half of every rule's alert volume is removed. That is the number
      behind a claim like "we cut alert volume in half", which is usually reported without it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid" role="list" aria-label="Headline figures">
    <div class="tile" role="listitem">
      <div class="n">{{ "%.1f"|format(stream.free_volume_pct) }}%</div>
      <div class="l">removable at zero loss</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tile" role="listitem">
      <div class="n">{{ "{:,.0f}".format(stream.free_hours) }}</div>
      <div class="l">analyst hours, at {{ stream.minutes_per_alert }} min per alert</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tile" role="listitem">
      <div class="n">{{ stream.untunable_rules | length }}</div>
      <div class="l">rules with no usable signal</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tile" role="listitem">
      <div class="n">{{ stream.unmeasured_rules | length }}</div>
      <div class="l">rules with too few detections to judge</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if charts.frontier %}
  <h2>The frontier</h2>
  <figure>
    <img src="{{ charts.frontier }}"
         alt="Line chart of true positives lost against alert volume removed, one line per rule. Rules with a usable signal bow below the diagonal; the rule with no usable signal tracks it.">
    <figcaption>
      Each line is one rule. The dotted diagonal is what tuning at random looks like: remove half the
      volume, lose half the detections. A line that bows below it is a rule worth tuning. A line on or
      above it is a rule being tuned by deleting detections.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  {% endif %}

  {% if charts.blanket %}
  <h2>What a blanket cut costs</h2>
  <figure>
    <img src="{{ charts.blanket }}"
         alt="Bar chart of true positives lost at each level of blanket volume reduction.">
    <figcaption>
      A flat percentage cut applied to every rule, including the ones that cannot be tuned. This is
      what an uncosted volume reduction target actually buys.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  {% endif %}

  <h2 id="rules">Per rule</h2>
  <table>
    <caption>
      Sorted by alert volume. Separation is the probability a random true positive outscores a random
      noise alert; 0.5 is no information. Tunability is decided by the interval, not the point
      estimate. A rule with fewer detections than the configured minimum reads "unknown" rather than
      "no": it needs a longer window, not a better signal.
    </caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Rule</th><th>Alerts</th><th>True pos.</th><th>Separation</th>
        <th>Removable free</th><th>Lost at 50%</th><th>Tunable</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for rule in rules %}
      <tr>
        <td><code>{{ rule.rule }}</code></td>
        <td>{{ "{:,}".format(rule.alerts) }}</td>
        <td>{{ rule.true_positives }}</td>
        <td>
          {{ "%.3f"|format(rule.separation) }}
          <div class="ci">[{{ "%.3f"|format(rule.separation_ci[0]) }}, {{ "%.3f"|format(rule.separation_ci[1]) }}]</div>
        </td>
        <td>
          {{ "%.1f"|format(rule.volume_removed_at_first_loss * 100) }}%
          <div class="ci">[{{ "%.1f"|format(rule.first_loss_ci[0] * 100) }}, {{ "%.1f"|format(rule.first_loss_ci[1] * 100) }}]</div>
        </td>
        <td>{{ "%.1f"|format(rule.loss_at['0.5'] * 100) }}%</td>
        {% if rule.verdict == "tunable" %}
        <td class="v v-yes">yes</td>
        {% elif rule.verdict == "not_tunable" %}
        <td class="v v-no">no</td>
        {% else %}
        <td class="v v-unknown">unknown</td>
        {% endif %}
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  {% if stream.rules_skipped_low_volume %}
  <h2>Skipped</h2>
  <p>
    Below the minimum volume to be worth tuning:
    {% for rule in stream.rules_skipped_low_volume %}<code>{{ rule }}</code> {% endfor %}
  </p>
  {% endif %}

  <footer>
    Intervals are {{ "%.0f"|format(95) }} percent bootstrap percentile intervals, stratified so every
    replicate holds the same number of true positives as the original.
    When the corpus is the bundled synthetic one, every number on this page is a simulation.
  </footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
